questions.questionText:
A # B means &lsquo;A is the brother of B&rsquo;

A @ B means &lsquo;A is the son of B&rsquo;

A &amp; B means &lsquo;A is the wife of B&rsquo;

A % B means &lsquo;A is the mother of B&rsquo;

If A % B &amp; C # D @ E, then how is B related to E?

questions.explanation:
Given series is G13D, J92K, ?, P91J, S71H.

To get the first element of the missing term,

G + 3 → J; J + 3 → **M**; M + 3 → P; P + 3 → S

For the second term:

13 → 1 + 3 = 4 → D;

92 → 9 + 2 = 11 → K;

**32** → 3 + 2 = 5 → E;

91 → 9 + 1 = 10 → J;

71 → 7 + 1 = 8 → H



Hence, the missing term is **M32E**.

Shortcut Trick

In any **triangle**, the angle formed by the **internal bisectors** of two angles (say &ang;B and &ang;C) at the **incenter** (I) is related to the third angle (&ang;A) by the formula:

Angle between bisectors = 90&deg; + (&ang;A &divide; 2)

Given &ang;A = 120&deg;

&rArr; Required Angle = 90&deg; + (120&deg; &divide; 2)

&rArr; Required Angle = 90&deg; + 60&deg; = 150&deg;

**&there4; The correct answer is 150&degree;.**

**Alternate Method**

**Given:**

One angle of the **triangle** (&ang;A) = 120&deg;

The other two angles are &ang;B and &ang;C.

**Property Used:** Sum of interior angles of a triangle is 180&deg;.

&rArr; In &Delta;ABC, &ang;A + &ang;B + &ang;C = 180&deg;

&rArr; 120&deg; + &ang;B + &ang;C = 180&deg;

&rArr; &ang;B + &ang;C = 180&deg; &minus; 120&deg; = 60&deg;

Let **I** be the point of intersection of the **bisectors** of &ang;B and &ang;C.

&rArr; In &Delta;BIC, the sum of angles is also 180&deg;:

&rArr; &ang;BIC + &ang;IBC + &ang;ICB = 180&deg;

&rArr; Since BI and CI are bisectors, &ang;IBC = &ang;B &divide; 2 and &ang;ICB = &ang;C &divide; 2.

&rArr; &ang;BIC + (&ang;B &divide; 2) + (&ang;C &divide; 2) = 180&deg;

&rArr; &ang;BIC + (&ang;B + &ang;C) &divide; 2 = 180&deg;

&rArr; &ang;BIC + (60&deg; &divide; 2) = 180&deg;

&rArr; &ang;BIC + 30&deg; = 180&deg;

&rArr; &ang;BIC = 180&deg; &minus; 30&deg; = 150&deg;

**&there4; The correct answer is 150&degree;.**

**Additional Information**

Incenter

The point where all internal **angle bisectors** of a triangle meet. It is the center of the **incircle**.

Angle at Excenter

The angle formed by the **external bisectors** of two angles of a triangle is given by the formula 90&deg; &minus; (&ang;A &divide; 2).

Angle in a Straight Line

Internal bisector and external bisector of the same angle are always **perpendicular** (form a 90&deg; angle) to each other.

26b:T12ce, Shortcut Trick

किसी भी **त्रिभुज** में, दो कोणों (मान लीजिए &ang;B और &ang;C) के **आंतरिक द्विभाजकों** द्वारा **अंतःकेंद्र** (I) पर बनने वाला कोण, तीसरे कोण (&ang;A) से निम्न सूत्र द्वारा संबंधित होता है:

द्विभाजकों के बीच का कोण = 90&deg; + (&ang;A &divide; 2)

दिया गया है &ang;A = 120&deg;

&rArr; आवश्यक कोण = 90&deg; + (120&deg; &divide; 2)

&rArr; आवश्यक कोण = 90&deg; + 60&deg; = 150&deg;

**&there4; सही उत्तर 150&deg; है।**

**Alternate Method**

**दिया गया है:**

**त्रिभुज** का एक कोण (&ang;A) = 120&deg;

अन्य दो कोण &ang;B और &ang;C हैं।

**प्रयुक्त गुण:** त्रिभुज के आंतरिक कोणों का योग 180&deg; होता है।

&rArr; &Delta;ABC में, &ang;A + &ang;B + &ang;C = 180&deg;

&rArr; 120&deg; + &ang;B + &ang;C = 180&deg;

&rArr; &ang;B + &ang;C = 180&deg; &minus; 120&deg; = 60&deg;

मान लीजिए **I**, &ang;B और &ang;C के **द्विभाजकों** का प्रतिच्छेदन बिंदु है।

&rArr; &Delta;BIC में, कोणों का योग भी 180&deg; है:

&rArr; &ang;BIC + &ang;IBC + &ang;ICB = 180&deg;

&rArr; चूंकि BI और CI द्विभाजक हैं, इसलिए &ang;IBC = &ang;B &divide; 2 और &ang;ICB = &ang;C &divide; 2 हैं।

&rArr; &ang;BIC + (&ang;B &divide; 2) + (&ang;C &divide; 2) = 180&deg;

&rArr; &ang;BIC + (&ang;B + &ang;C) &divide; 2 = 180&deg;

&rArr; &ang;BIC + (60&deg; &divide; 2) = 180&deg;

&rArr; &ang;BIC + 30&deg; = 180&deg;

&rArr; &ang;BIC = 180&deg; &minus; 30&deg; = 150&deg;

**&there4; सही उत्तर 150&deg; है।**

**Additional Information**

अंतःकेंद्र (Incenter)

वह बिंदु जहाँ त्रिभुज के सभी आंतरिक **कोण द्विभाजक** मिलते हैं। यह **अंतःवृत्त** का केंद्र होता है।

बहिःकेंद्र पर कोण (Angle at Excenter)

त्रिभुज के दो कोणों के **बाह्य द्विभाजकों** द्वारा निर्मित कोण सूत्र 90&deg; &minus; (&ang;A &divide; 2) द्वारा दिया जाता है।

एक सीधी रेखा में कोण

एक ही कोण के आंतरिक द्विभाजक और बाह्य द्विभाजक हमेशा एक-दूसरे के **लंबवत** (90&deg; का कोण बनाते हैं) होते हैं।

26c:T5f9,**ఉపయోగించిన కాన్సెప్ట్:**

&Delta;ABCలో, BO మరియు CO కోణ ద్విభాగాలు అయితే, అప్పుడు &ang;BOC = 90 + 1/2&ang;A

**సాధన:**

ఇచ్చిన చిత్రం ప్రకారం, BO మరియు CO కోణ ద్విభాగాలు మరియు ద్విభాగాల మధ్య కోణం &ang;BOC,

&ang;BOC = 90 + 1/2 &ang;BAC = 90 + 1/2 × 120 = 90 + 60 = 150&deg; 

&there4; **సరైన సమాధానం 150&deg;**
